@startuml
title Loopin — Kanban Task State Chart
hide empty description
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #FFF45C
  BorderColor #222222
  FontColor #111111
  RoundCorner 18
}
skinparam ArrowColor #222222
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.2
skinparam StateFontSize 14
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #EEF3FA
skinparam NoteBorderColor #587DA8
skinparam noteFontSize 11

[*] --> NotCreated : task creation requested

state "Not Created" as NotCreated
state "Task exists in project board" as Existing {
  state "TODO list" as TODO
  state "IN_PROGRESS list" as InProgress
  state "DONE list" as Done
  state "CUSTOM list" as Custom

  [*] --> TODO : created in TODO list
  [*] --> InProgress : created in IN_PROGRESS list
  [*] --> Done : created in DONE list
  [*] --> Custom : created in CUSTOM list

  TODO --> InProgress : drop / move\n[newList.projectId == task.projectId]
  TODO --> Done : move / CLI task done\n[target list is DONE]
  TODO --> Custom : move\n[same project]
  InProgress --> TODO : move\n[same project]
  InProgress --> Done : move / CLI task done\n[same project]
  InProgress --> Custom : move\n[same project]
  Done --> TODO : reopen / move\n[same project]
  Done --> InProgress : move\n[same project]
  Done --> Custom : move\n[same project]
  Custom --> TODO : move\n[same project]
  Custom --> InProgress : move\n[same project]
  Custom --> Done : move / CLI task done\n[same project]
  Custom --> Custom : reorder / move within or across custom lists\n[same project]

  TODO --> TODO : reorder / update position
  InProgress --> InProgress : reorder / update position
  Done --> Done : reorder / update position

  TODO --> TODO : edit title / description / stack / priority / due date
  InProgress --> InProgress : edit title / description / stack / priority / due date
  Done --> Done : edit title / description / stack / priority / due date
  Custom --> Custom : edit task details

  TODO --> TODO : assign / unassign\n[assignee is ACTIVE project member]
  InProgress --> InProgress : assign / unassign\n[assignee is ACTIVE project member]
  Done --> Done : assign / unassign\n[assignee is ACTIVE project member]
  Custom --> Custom : assign / unassign\n[assignee is ACTIVE project member]

  TODO --> TODO : associate commit\n[commit belongs to project]
  InProgress --> InProgress : associate commit\n[commit belongs to project]
  Done --> Done : associate commit\n[commit belongs to project]
  Custom --> Custom : associate commit\n[commit belongs to project]
}

NotCreated --> TODO : persist Task\n[requester is ACTIVE member]
NotCreated --> Custom : persist Task\n[requester is ACTIVE member]
NotCreated --> InProgress : persist Task\n[requester is ACTIVE member]
NotCreated --> Done : persist Task\n[requester is ACTIVE member]

TODO --> Deleted : delete task\n[requester is ACTIVE member]
InProgress --> Deleted : delete task\n[requester is ACTIVE member]
Done --> Deleted : delete task\n[requester is ACTIVE member]
Custom --> Deleted : delete task\n[requester is ACTIVE member]
state "Deleted" as Deleted
Deleted --> [*]

TODO --> TODO : rejected move\n[different project / 400]
InProgress --> InProgress : rejected move\n[different project / 400]
Done --> Done : rejected move\n[different project / 400]
Custom --> Custom : rejected move\n[different project / 400]

note right of Existing
Task fields persisted by Task:
title, description, position, stack,
priority, dueDate, listId, projectId,
assigneeId?, commitId?, createdAt,
updatedAt.

A task's visible column is derived from
its List.kind / listId association.
end note

note bottom of Existing
Guards:
- requester must be an ACTIVE project member
- assignee, when set, must be ACTIVE in same project
- destination list must belong to same project
- move and position update run transactionally
end note

note left of TODO
Task creation starts at the selected List.
The list's kind is not inferred from its
display name.
end note

note right of Done
CLI:
loopin task done [taskId]
moves to a list whose title matches
Done / Finish / Completed; otherwise
uses the last list as fallback.
end note

@enduml